{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/pacer/src/rate-limiter.ts#L156","children":[{"type":"text","value":"rate-limiter.ts:156"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A class that creates a rate-limited function."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rate limiting is a simple approach that allows a function to execute up to a limit within a time window,\nthen blocks all subsequent calls until the window passes. This can lead to \"bursty\" behavior where\nall executions happen immediately, followed by a complete block.\nThis synchronous version is lighter weight and often all you need - upgrade to AsyncRateLimiter when you need promises, retry support, abort capabilities, or advanced error handling."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The rate limiter supports two types of windows:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"'fixed': A strict window that resets after the window period. All executions within the window count\ntowards the limit, and the window resets completely after the period."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"'sliding': A rolling window that allows executions as old ones expire. This provides a more\nconsistent rate of execution over time."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For smoother execution patterns, consider using:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Throttling: Ensures consistent spacing between executions (e.g. max once per 200ms)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debouncing: Waits for a pause in calls before executing (e.g. after 500ms of no calls)"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rate limiting is best used for hard API limits or resource constraints. For UI updates or\nsmoothing out frequent events, throttling or debouncing usually provide better user experience."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State Management:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Uses TanStack Store for reactive state management"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialState"},{"type":"text","value":" to provide initial state values when creating the rate limiter"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onExecute"},{"type":"text","value":" callback to react to function execution and implement custom logic"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onReject"},{"type":"text","value":" callback to react to executions being rejected when rate limit is exceeded"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The state includes execution count, execution times, and rejection count"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State can be accessed via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rateLimiter.store.state"},{"type":"text","value":" when using the class directly"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When using framework adapters (React/Solid), state is accessed from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rateLimiter.state"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const rateLimiter = new RateLimiter(\n  (id: string) => api.getData(id),\n  {\n    limit: 5,\n    window: 1000,\n    windowType: 'sliding',\n  }\n);\n\n// Will execute immediately until limit reached, then block\nrateLimiter.maybeExecute('123');","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/AnyFunction.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyFunction"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"constructors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Constructors"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"constructor","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Constructor"}]},{"type":"code","value":"new RateLimiter<TFn>(fn, initialOptions): RateLimiter<TFn>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/pacer/src/rate-limiter.ts#L163","children":[{"type":"text","value":"rate-limiter.ts:163"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"initialoptions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"initialOptions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/RateLimiterOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RateLimiterOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"parag